  "summary": "Metal Slug X is SNK's reworking of Metal Slug 2, released for Neo Geo MVS in March 1999.",
  "body": [
    "Metal Slug X is SNK's reworking of Metal Slug 2, released for Neo Geo MVS in March 1999. Marco, Tarma, Eri and Fio return to the same broad campaign against Morden and an alien threat, but revised encounters and presentation change the route through it. The game keeps the run-and-gun structure of infantry fighting, found weapons and rideable machines. Its revised engine addresses the earlier release's severe slowdown, making the difference apparent in crowded scenes where the player must keep reading attacks and moving through them.",
    "Changes to enemy placement, weapons and the stages' appearance make knowledge of the previous version useful without guaranteeing that an encounter will unfold in exactly the same way. A familiar stretch can introduce another threat or a different opportunity to collect equipment. The central decisions remain immediate: whether to stay inside a vehicle, use a powerful weapon now or preserve it for the next large enemy. The remix works within that established vocabulary, adjusting what appears and when so the campaign develops another rhythm under the player's hands.",
    "The detailed character animation and destructible scenery remain central to the spectacle. Prisoners, soldiers and machines react throughout the action, giving a short exchange a comic detail alongside its practical danger. Transformations and the enlarged four-character cast also carry over from Metal Slug 2. The relationship between the releases makes X an unusual sequel-era landmark: its identity comes from revisiting an existing adventure and altering the performance, pacing and encounters enough to give that familiar journey another life in the arcade."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "The second campaign remixed",
    "A familiar place, another threat",
    "A new version with its own rhythm"
  ],
